12) Testing pyramid, all on Linux except the last item:
(a) a unit test file per system using a tiny world-builder DSL;
(b) an invariant checker run after every tick in tests and debug builds: ledger conservation (Δtreasury = Σ ledger postings, with declared sources and sinks), population ≥ 0, manpower ≤ cap, stability in [0,1], no NaN or Inf in any Double column, valid owners and handles, ring buffers bounded;
(c) seeded property and fuzz tests: random valid and invalid command streams for 1–5 years, where invariants hold and rejected commands leave the state hash unchanged;
(d) determinism and cross-arch hash tests;
(e) golden saves and replays;
(f) nightly 50-year all-AI balance runs over 5 seeds via `simcli balance`. They emit CSV and chart artifacts and assert sanity bands: world GDP real growth 1–5%/yr, world population within ±15% of the real trajectory for the same years, no country's debt above 300% of GDP for 10+ years, the largest power's share of world GDP below 40%, rebellions and war counts within bands;
(g) a tick-time benchmark gate;
(h) on macOS only: a simulator smoke UI test (launch, pick a country, run 30 days, screenshot artifact) and an IPA gate checking Payload/*.app contains every manifest file with matching SHA-256, an arm64 executable, MinimumOSVersion 17.0, landscape-only orientations, UIDeviceFamily [1], and size limits.
